    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Seiya Suzuki** (67.36) and **Corbin Carroll** (64.88) headline our production expectations. **Seiya Suzuki** benefits from a massive 16% SP skill adjustment against Seth Lugo, while **Corbin Carroll** remains a priority start despite Yamamoto\u2019s presence; the high-volume SB opportunity, even against a tougher arm, is non-negotiable for our team\u2019s statistical goals. We are also leaning heavily on **Brice Turang** (64.10) and **Isaac Paredes** (64.27). **Brice Turang** is a high-upside play at the top of the order against Taj Bradley, where his speed metrics combined with the SP's slow delivery provide a significant leg up on our scarcest category. **Isaac Paredes** remains locked into our corner infield spot, thriving on a strong platoon advantage against a mid-rotation arm in Mitch King.\n\nWe faced a tight squeeze on the bubble, ultimately opting to keep **Cole Young** (39.56) on the bench. He hovered just below our 40-point efficiency floor, as the matchup against Griffin Jax offered too little resistance to justify bumping a higher-scored bat. Meanwhile, **Max Muncy** (62.89) makes the lineup despite a poor batting order placement thanks to a favorable wind-out environment and a 7% boost from his platoon edge. We are monitoring **Zach McKinstry** (42.77) closely; he remains in the lineup by the slimmest of margins, as the wind-out factor marginally offsets the drag of a 9th-hole assignment. \n\nRisks are concentrated around our high-end talent facing elite arms. **Gabriel Moreno** (53.37) and **Austin Riley** (48.58) are both navigating difficult matchups against Yamamoto and Gerrit Cole, respectively. While both are strictly marginal plays today, their presence is necessitated by our desire to maximize plate appearances without cratering our efficiency. **Jose Caballero** (52.65) is our \"wildcard\" start\u2014while the matchup against Chris Sale is objectively daunting (resulting in a -19% SP skill penalty), the 13% boost from the platoon advantage and his elite speed profile forces his inclusion. We will continue to track the status of **James Wood** and **Giancarlo Stanton** on the IL as we look to return to full strength.",
